@ [date] 2026-09-02
@ [design_uuid] f76ce32a-e1a7-4b9b-8fa1-339057be7adf
@ [P6_implementation_commit] b08837ae0bdb56c27c4adc3786b07b2e72072cd5

& [ReadinessConclusion]
  + T3 compact manifest T4 manifest receipt and T5 host-checked treatments are now technically available and clean-replayed
  + the next missing substrate is a deterministic provider-independent case generator renderer answer-key vault and scorer
  + no external model run or provider spend is authorized by this readiness record

& [MinimumCaseFamily]
  + basket sizes are 2 8 and 32
  + every case uses one shared object type two overlapping labels one exact handle query one ambiguous-label query one current-state query one patch and one stale replay attempt
  + the 8 and 32 member cases place the target near the beginning middle and end under counterbalanced case seeds
  + one decoy shares the target label role and purpose but differs in one exact state or differentiator
  + every generated source fact is treatment invariant and every treatment receives the same task order

& [GeneratorOutputSeparation]
  + public_case contains seed declared facts patch chronology and tasks without expected answers
  + private_answer_key contains complete handle set exact current records ambiguity sets permitted Unknown outcomes expected changed handle unchanged handles and stale-refusal result
  + treatment_projection contains T0 prose T1 handles T2 full register T3 manifest plus materialization T4 receipt obligation and T5 host route without altering source facts
  + generation_receipt binds all three outputs to one case digest while never placing answer-key fields in a model prompt

& [RequiredModelAnswerForm]
  + enumerated_handles is an ordered unique list
  + resolutions map each query to Resolved Ambiguous or Unknown and exact candidate handles when applicable
  + state_answers cite one exact handle generation and value or Unresolved
  + proposed_update names target expected version expected ledger digest and declared unchanged handles
  + attention_dispositions cover every supplied manifest member for T4 and T5
  + prose explanation is optional and never overrides the scored structured fields

& [DeterministicScorer]
  + membership true positive false positive false negative and duplicate counts are computed from exact SemanticIds
  + resolution distinguishes correct exact resolution correct ambiguity correct unknown identity swap ambiguity collapse and invention
  + state scoring distinguishes current predecessor foreign-member and unsupported values
  + mutation scoring distinguishes correct target collateral mutation stale acceptance and protocol bypass
  + receipt scoring distinguishes complete exact coverage justified Held unresolved laundering and Relevant without materialization
  + malformed or missing structured output remains a scored failure rather than being repaired by evaluator inference

& [RunPhases]
  + P0 provider-independent harness validation uses generated cases renderers host calls and deliberately corrupted synthetic answers only
  + P1 smoke uses two case seeds per basket-treatment cell and exists to detect prompt schema provider and scorer faults without hypothesis claims
  + P2 preregistered minimum uses at least twenty fresh case seeds per basket-treatment cell after freezing generator renderer scorer model settings and thresholds
  + P3 qualitative failure inspection begins only after aggregate P2 artifacts and metrics are sealed

& [PrimaryComparisons]
  + T0 to T1 estimates stable-handle contribution
  + T1 to T2 estimates complete structured roster contribution
  + T2 to T3 tests accuracy retention against measured context savings
  + T3 to T4 estimates explicit disposition-accounting contribution
  + T4 to T5 estimates host enforcement contribution with acceptance-conditioned and total utility both reported

& [PreRegistrationRules]
  + primary endpoint is total identity integrity error count comprising swap false merge false split omission invention stale dereference collateral mutation ambiguity collapse unresolved laundering and protocol bypass
  + secondary endpoints are exact membership F1 resolution calibration current-state accuracy complete-receipt rate held-when-required rate bytes latency and host-call count
  + success is not one arbitrary percentage; report per-case paired deltas bootstrap confidence intervals by seed and the complete error distribution by basket size
  + a treatment that gains correctness mainly by refusal must report both accepted-work correctness and total attempted-work utility
  + P2 cannot reuse P1 seeds or change prompts scoring settings or thresholds after outputs are inspected

& [ImplementationBoundary]
  + generator renderer scorer and synthetic-answer fixtures require a separately signed evaluation specification before Rust implementation
  + provider adapter model selection credentials budgets rate limits and external calls remain separately authorized runtime concerns
  + raw prompts outputs settings timings host responses and scorer results must be retained without private chain-of-thought requests

& [MostImportantFalsifier]
  + if T3 preserves bytes but degrades identity accuracy against T2 at the same tasks the manifest is hiding cues the model needs and materialization policy must be redesigned
  + if T4 adds output without improving errors calibration or held behavior the receipt is bureaucracy rather than an effective attention intervention
  + if T5 only improves results by refusing nearly everything objective attention needs better task decomposition or retrieval rather than stronger gates

& [RecommendedNext]
  + preserve source and form the provider-independent generator renderer scorer specification only; do not contact a model provider until the harness defeats corrupted synthetic answers deterministically
